# Example ReRDMFT input file: carbon monoxide (R = 1.128 Angstrom), 6-31G basis (co-6-31g.gbs, from
# https://www.basissetexchange.org/), GNOF (3 coupling subspaces of 2 orbitals), 4-component with the MIN-MAX stage
# (FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG), NEO and CHOLESKY TRUE. RKB basis of 72 spinors (36 negative-energy, 36 positive-energy).
# The first stage is the no-pair minimization over the positive-energy spinors (-112.9253463 Ha). FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG
# TRUE then continues from that minimum with rotations that also mix the 20 occupied positive-energy spinors
# (occupation > 1e-6) with the 36 negative-energy ones: NEO converges the orbitals to the saddle point of order 720
# (energy maximized along those electron-positron directions, minimized along the rest), alternating with the full
# re-minimization of the occupation numbers. Measured: ~75 s in total, the min-max stage takes 2 macro-iterations and
# moves the energy by 1e-9 Ha. The check of the saddle type (dense diagonalization of the Hessian and count of its
# negative eigenvalues: 720 expected) runs only with DEBUG TRUE and adds ~2 minutes at this size.
# Follow the run with `tail -f co_631g_c4_gnof_neg_neo_cholesky.live`.
NELEC 14
BASIS co-6-31g.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 3
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG TRUE
ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO
CHOLESKY TRUE

GEOMETRY
C   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
O   0.000000   0.000000   1.128000
END
